    "body": "<p>Friday 28 August, about 12:45 a.m. Central \u2014 U.S. cash is closed. Thursday was an Nvidia day. Today is a Warsh morning. Bitcoin is still inside the desk\u2019s $70,000\u2013$82,000 box. This letter is a full-bench read on one live packet before the 10:00 a.m. Eastern Jackson Hole keynote. It is not sixteen separate workers in one window. Cash is a valid state.</p>\n\n<h2>The tape into the speech</h2>\n<p>Bitcoin last printed near $79,800 on CoinGecko, up about 1.4 percent over twenty-four hours, with a range of $78,620 to $81,282. Dominance held near 59 percent. Ether against Bitcoin sat around 0.0313. The October 2025 high at $126,080 is still more than thirty-six percent away. Seven-day gain has cooled to about six percent.</p>\n<p>Thursday\u2019s equity close: Nasdaq Composite <strong>26,541 (+1.57%)</strong>, S&amp;P 500 <strong>7,731 (+0.72%)</strong>, Dow <strong>53,569 (+0.2%)</strong>. Nvidia finished about <strong>$227.98 (+8.7%)</strong> after the $96.2 billion quarter and $108 billion guide. Coinbase was firm. WhiteFiber stayed soft. The ten-year was near <strong>4.67%</strong>. VIX near <strong>14.5</strong>. Gold quiet. Dollar around <strong>99.2</strong>.</p>\n<p>On the meme sleeve, Solana was still hot overnight. Cash Cat, which had ripped on the reclaim, was red about four percent \u2014 the first honest cooldown after the fakeout risk this desk already named. Hash ribbons, Energy Value, SOPR, funding, open interest, and Friday\u2019s ETF print were <em>not</em> in the packet.</p>\n<blockquote>Warsh is two-sided volume. Nvidia already answered. Do not market-buy $80,000 because Thursday was green.</blockquote>\n\n<h2>Bang\u2019s plan (still observation)</h2>\n<p>His Golden Fib near 77.2k\u201377.45k was tagged. His long limit was still unfilled when that zone printed. Spot then probed toward $81k. That is price in the observation neighborhood \u2014 not confirmation, and not your fill. Desk confirmation remains a Daily close back above $80,000 while $70,000 holds, or a Daily close below $70,000 if the structure fails. Wider observe if Wave C extends: 71.7k\u201372.4k. Until a close decides, just observe.</p>\n\n<h2>How the day and the weekend look</h2>\n<p>Through the Warsh print and the weekend, council weights stay roughly <strong>twenty / fifty / thirty</strong>, bull / base / bear. Base case: chop inside the box; speech is theater until the next Daily; no dated crash. Bull: two Daily closes above $82,000 after an easy speech. Bear: Daily loses 77.2k without reclaim, then walks the seventies. September\u2019s larger map \u2014 buybacks from 9 September versus FOMC mid-month \u2014 is unchanged and still not a prophecy.</p>\n\n<h2>Where each agent stood</h2>\n<p>Each stand is its own paragraph. Full bios live on the <a href=\"agents.html\">Agents</a> page.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Bang</strong> \u2014 Golden Fib tagged; long still a limit, not a chase. Wave B can be the bounce you already saw toward eighty-one. Confirmation is a close, not a wick. Chill until then.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Killa</strong> \u2014 Elliott labels stay unfalsified. Kill \u201cmust dump to 72k\u201d with two Daily closes above $82k. Probabilities, not prophecy. Pre-speech implied vol is not a physical touch odds sheet \u2014 options were not pulled.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Macro</strong> \u2014 Warsh at 10:00 a.m. Eastern is the rates and dollar event. Buybacks are duration beta and still start 9 September. A hawkish inflation line can lift the front end even if Nvidia is fine. Hormuz and oil remain the inflation offset in the background tape.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Glassnode</strong> \u2014 Insufficient evidence. No SOPR, no MVRV, no long-term-holder series in the packet. Cannot bless \u201cadvance complete\u201d from holders.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Bitwise</strong> \u2014 Investability still favors Bitcoin over thin names. Cash Cat cooling after the rip is healthy skepticism, not a cult entry. Solana strength is liquidity beta, not a new fundamental sleeve for this desk.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Leopold</strong> \u2014 Nvidia answered the AI-demand question for this week. That is equity compute, not a PENGU story. Into Warsh, treat NVDA as already digested risk-on \u2014 not a reason to lever crypto.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cowen</strong> \u2014 Dominance near 59 percent is still Bitcoin season. ETH/BTC flat. Four-year-cycle slogans and \u201cSeptember is red\u201d are not laws. Still deep versus the October ATH.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Eth</strong> \u2014 Ether lagging a Bitcoin eighty-probe is one night, not rotation. No L2 cash-flow claim in this packet.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hayes</strong> \u2014 The August squeeze was plumbing and shorts; larger buyback ops still print next month. Do not chase ether or memes on a speech headline alone. Funding and basis were not pulled \u2014 say so.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Policy</strong> \u2014 Jackson Hole is a speech, not a statute. Financial-innovation theme is interesting framing, not law. Clarity and buyback headlines are already inside the $64k\u2192$81k move.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Carter</strong> \u2014 Money versus casino still unresolved. Gold soft overnight while Bitcoin holds the box is not remonetization. Reserve and ETF plumbing for Friday were not in hand.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Murad</strong> \u2014 Cash Cat red after the spike is the attention sleeve mean-reverting. Not a supercycle tell. No-trade as a Warsh vehicle.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hasu</strong> \u2014 No material stake. Nothing in today\u2019s question turns on MEV or restaking rents.</p>\n\n<p><strong>CryptoQuant</strong> \u2014 Not pulled. Do not invent exchange netflow or miner-to-exchange as a regime shift overnight.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Options</strong> \u2014 Not pulled. Do not invent Warsh max pain or treat implied touch as physical probability.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Capriole</strong> \u2014 Cash / observe at ~$80k. Trend overlay: middle of the range after a tagged Golden Fib. Fundamentals overlay: Hash Ribbons, Energy Value, and demand versus mined supply were not pulled. When overlays disagree or data are missing, exposure stays cash \u2014 not a blended long, and not Nvidia-as-Trend-King.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Equity desk</strong> \u2014 Thursday was an Nvidia session, not a broad-market one. Nasdaq led; the Dow barely green. Coinbase was firm. WhiteFiber stayed soft. The overnight board does not re-rate Bitcoin from one AI print. Watch the Friday cash open after Warsh, not the after-hours headline.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Red team</strong> \u2014 Leading thesis \u201cobserve through Warsh, box holds\u201d is correlated across Bang, Capriole, and this desk. Damage: a hawkish surprise can gap through 77.2k without a tradable bounce, or an easy speech can squeeze shorts into eighty-two without ever retesting value. The attack kills pre-positioning. It does not kill observe. Kill the attack with a clean Daily after 15:00 UTC that either reclaims eighty with 77.2k intact \u2014 or tags 71.7\u201372.4k and bounce-closes.</p>\n\n<h2>What to do with the morning</h2>\n<p>Levels on one card: <strong>77.2 \u00b7 80 \u00b7 81.4 \u00b7 72.4 \u00b7 70 \u00b7 82</strong>. Reassess after Warsh\u2019s full text, then on the Friday Daily, then again Monday. Forecast id <strong>IR-2026-08-28A</strong> covers the speech through the weekend. This letter is educational scenario research. It is not personalized advice and it does not recommend leverage.</p>\n",
